= Cross-Party Outreach

Divided government requires deals, and deals require relationships across the aisle.

- @gop_moderates: Cultivate Republican moderates
- @business_groups: Meet with business leaders
- @governors: Work with Republican governors
- @easy_discard

@gop_moderates
on-arrival: gopmod_relation += 8; moderate_strength += 2; progressive_dissent += 3; suburban_dem += 1*(1-dissent); month_actions += 1

Quiet dinners and joint bills build trust.

@business_groups
on-arrival: biz_relation += 8; moderate_strength += 1; labor_dissent += 3; resources += 1; month_actions += 1

Chambers of commerce and tech executives are courted; some are even friendly.

@governors
on-arrival: gopmod_relation += 5; dem_governors += 0; rural_dem += 1*(1-dissent); suburban_dem += 1*(1-dissent); institutions += 1; month_actions += 1

Practical state-level cooperation offers a model for national dealmaking.
